 one of the  first things we did was uh  me and a couple of writers were just  kind of brainstorming like okay what are  the like the dumbest spell balls these  guys could have because  because um i think one of the things we  wanted to do with the magic was to show  that a lot of the centaurs didn't use  them for anything purposeful it was just  for things that like why would this  exist  and um a writer uh my friend hannah  hannah friedman  um we were coming up with the names you  know things like handsome for eight  seconds just these really  names of these all these spells um i  think she pitched one of them as being i  can shoot tiny versions of myself from  my hooves  and that was um and that one just stuck  we just we laughed so much and i started  drawing out the visuals for it  and as i did i was thinking i would  realize that  whatever you know like this would be  like birthing new life  and that it you know like we just  imagine there would be a moment of  existential horror so it just became a  thing  that we had we had um that just stuck  and and so we had them do this  repeatedly  um but it was it was something that was  conceived at the very beginning in  development and we just always  you know like found different ways to  insert it in there because it was such a  bizarre idea  i've been always like fascinated by by  the movement towards more  uh serialization in in in cartoons  and especially in recent years so as  that and  [Music]  the show has like a unique blend like uh  each episode his own thing but also like  he has a  a narrative arc uh was that a part of  the  initial uh concept or did that come in  later how was that like  um that was also part of the the initial  concept um  i uh and um it's interesting how it  relates  to the music as well because we're sort  of thinking of it like  if you have a season it could be almost  like the season like its own album but  then each episode could also be like  their own mini chapters or albums as  well  and um uh yeah so we were thinking about  it in relation to the music but also  um i i really wanted it to to be um  something that had  um um like  a just a feeling of just that kind of  fairy tale quality just being a bigger  story  um and uh i i  really loved um growing up i loved  things like i love all puppets you know  like the muppets  and all of that are a big influence but  um but other  like kinds of like henson projects like  um like  you know like labyrinth and dark crystal  things that had like you know a lot of  different things tonally going on but  that were these kinds of  cool bigger stories the neverending  story all of that  um i wanted something that really just  kind of  was you know felt like it was a big  bigger continuous story um  lastly i know you probably can't say  much about the future of the show  but is there anything uh from this  season that you would really hope  uh to explore further in uh in a  possible season two or anything  yeah um i mean i i think after  establishing this world  um i would love to you know kind of take  it to different  different places kind of meet different  centaurs find different communities that  we haven't  um haven't met yet and kind of areas  that we haven't explored  um but but also um i i really want to  uh show more of the the lore and the  backstory or what you know like we've  alluded to a lot of like what's been  going on here why there's so much  darkness in addition to all the  um the absurdity of the show um so  getting kind of exploring more of the  history of it  is something that i'd love to do now  that you mentioned that uh  let um do you mentioned like the  the big like fantasy movie that sort of  inspired you  but how was um when you went to actually  riding that lauren and  how did you guys find the balancing how  much to these of these  larger uh history or even like the  mystery of it all  without it overtaking the like the  individual episode storylines  yeah um that's a great question because  because there was uh there was a lot to  balance with it  and um uh yeah i did write a lot of the  history and the lore  first and and it was kind of going in  and kind of  making sure that it didn't overtake too  much of the story it was  it was always tricky kind of calibrating  that part of it because there's so much  there's so many questions  to be answered but but really at the  heart of it we're following  horse through this journey and we always  had to keep in mind this is from her  lens and this and her  her journey emotionally is the most  important thing so that's kind of how we  we um knew when to like lift out stuff  that was  that got too much into the history  because it's always about her and where  she's at  her search for writer um so so i think  prioritizing the emotional  the emotional arc was always most  important for us  well meg it's been a pleasure talking to  you thank you so much and huge  congratulations on the show  thank you thank you so much
 

